<title>CANADA: Alberta combines 10 pct of crop vs 7 pct last year.</title>
<headline>Alberta combines 10 pct of crop vs 7 pct last year.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberta Wheat Pool said on Friday that 10 percent of Alberta crops were combined by August 30 compared with seven percent at the same time last year.</p>
<p>CROP		  PCT COMBINED TO DATE  PCT COMBINED LAST YEAR</p>
<p>Hard Red Spring Wheat	 6			   5</p>
<p>Canada Prairie S. Wheat     3			   2</p>
<p>Soft White S. Wheat	  25			  12</p>
<p>Winter Wheat		   88			  67</p>
<p>Durum Wheat		    24			  13</p>
<p>Oats				6			   4</p>
<p>Barley			   14			   8</p>
<p>Flax				2			   2</p>
<p>Fall Rye			 56			  66</p>
<p>Canola			   11			   4</p>
<p>Total			    10			   7</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
